{"id":"CVE-2008-5031","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2008-11-10T16:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T10:40:17.351Z","description":"Multiple integer overflows in Python 2.2.3 through 2.5.1, and 2.6, allow context-dependent attackers to have an unknown impact via a large integer value in the tabsize argument to the expandtabs method, as implemented by (1) the string_expandtabs function in Objects/stringobject.c and (2) the unicode_expandtabs function in Objects/unicodeobject.c.  NOTE: this vulnerability reportedly exists because of an incomplete fix for CVE-2008-2315.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://svn.python.org/view/python/trunk/Objects/unicodeobject.c?rev=61350&view=diff&r1=61350&r2=61349&p1=python/trunk/Objects/unicodeobject.c&p2=/python/trunk/Objects/unicodeobject.c","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://security.gentoo.org/glsa/glsa-200907-16.xml","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-200907-16"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/33937","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"33937"},{"url":"http://scary.beasts.org/security/CESA-2008-008.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/37471","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"37471"},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2008/11/05/3","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[oss-security] 20081105 Re: CVE Request - Python string expandtabs"},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2008/11/05/2","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[oss-security] 20081105 CVE Request - Python string expandtabs"},{"url":"http://www.vmware.com/security/advisories/VMSA-2009-0016.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://support.apple.com/kb/HT3438","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://svn.python.org/view?rev=61350&view=rev","tags":["x_